Micropolis for Ubuntu
=====================

This package runs Micropolis as a self-contained local web application.
/usr/games/micropolis starts an HTTP server bound only to 127.0.0.1 and opens
the game in the user's default browser. The packaged application itself does
not require an external web application service.

The launcher normally uses port 48080. Keeping a stable port is intentional:
browser-managed site data is scoped to an origin, which includes the port. If
another application owns that port, Micropolis exits with an error rather than
silently selecting a different origin. An alternate port can be selected with
--port, with the consequence that browser-stored settings or saved state may
appear separate.

Architecture coverage
---------------------

The installed web application is CPU-independent. Nevertheless the binary
package is deliberately declared Architecture: any so Launchpad performs a
real package build and smoke test on each enabled Ubuntu architecture instead
of producing a single Architecture: all binary. This is specifically intended
to exercise amd64, i386, arm64, armhf, ppc64el, riscv64 and s390x builders when
the target series publishes those architectures.

